 "selfTest": 2500,
 "_about": "Vintage Cyan: Vintage's LCD from 1985 in cyan fluorescent readouts on dark teal windows: the rpm as a dot-matrix band (ghost dots unlit, orange from 5200, red from 6750) over a tick scale with dot-matrix numbers; the slanted seven-segment speed over ghost 8s, an amber TURBO lamp over a boost bar (0-1.6 bar, rising segments) to its left and the ECON bar to its right (green filling left while driving economically, red filling right under load: hud.js econEco / econLoad); oil / water / fuel bars, P R N D S M and the gear; three dot-matrix strips along the bottom (the outside temperature; the range and average speed; the clock); the roundel in the theme's colours; scanlines, and a 2.5 s self-test at power-on. Made by cluster-design/vintage2/build.html?v=cyan. km/h and °C are drawn into the face: pick metric units. Widget reference: shared/hud.js header.",
